        <div class="docs-header">
            <h1 class="docs-title"><i class="fas fa-dice-d20" style="color: var(--color-primary-400);"></i> D&D 5e RPG System Guide</h1>
            <p class="docs-subtitle">Complete guide to the Discord RPG adventure system powered by AI</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick Start -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="quickstart">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-rocket" style="color: var(--color-success-400);"></i> Quick Start</h2>
            <p>Get started with D&D 5e in 3 simple steps!</p>

            <h3>1. Create a Character</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg character create name:Thorin class:fighter species:dwarf background:soldier</div>

            <h3>2. Start an Adventure</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg session start</div>

            <h3>3. Take Actions</h3>
            <p>After starting, just type what you want to do:</p>
            <div class="info-box">
                <strong>Example Actions:</strong><br>
                "I search the room for hidden doors"<br>
                "I attack the goblin with my sword"<br>
                "I try to persuade the guard to let us pass"
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Character Creation -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="character">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-user-shield" style="color: var(--color-purple-400);"></i> Character Creation</h2>

            <h3>Classes (12 Available)</h3>
            <p>Barbarian, Bard, Cleric, Druid, Fighter, Monk, Paladin, Ranger, Rogue, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard</p>

            <h3>Races (30+ Supported)</h3>
            <p>Human, Elf, Dwarf, Halfling, Dragonborn, Gnome, Half-Elf, Half-Orc, Tiefling, Aasimar, Goliath, Tabaxi, Kenku, Firbolg, Kobold, Lizardfolk, Tortle, Warforged, Changeling, Genasi, and more!</p>

            <h3>Backgrounds (15 Available)</h3>
            <p>Acolyte, Criminal, Folk Hero, Noble, Sage, Soldier, Charlatan, Entertainer, Guild Artisan, Hermit, Outlander, Sailor, Spy, Urchin</p>

            <div class="success-box">
                <strong><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Tip:</strong> Each background grants 2 skill proficiencies!
            </div>

            <h3>Racial Bonuses (Auto-Applied)</h3>
            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>Dwarf</h4>
                    <p>+2 CON, Darkvision, Dwarven Resilience</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>Elf</h4>
                    <p>+2 DEX, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>Human</h4>
                    <p>+1 to all ability scores</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-card">
                    <h4>Tiefling</h4>
                    <p>+2 CHA, +1 INT, Darkvision, Hellish Resistance</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stat Rolling -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="statrolling">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-dice" style="color: var(--color-warning-400);"></i> Stat Rolling Methods</h2>
            <p>Three ways to generate your ability scores!</p>

            <h3>Option 1: Roll for Stats (Classic D&D)</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg statroll roll</div>
            <p>Rolls 4d6, drops the lowest die, 6 times.</p>
            <div class="info-box">
                <strong>Example:</strong> Roll 1: [6, 5, 4, 2] → 6+5+4 = <span class="success-text"><strong>15</strong></span> (dropped 2)
            </div>

            <h3>Option 2: Standard Array</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg statroll standard</div>
            <p>Use the balanced array: <strong class="success-text">15, 14, 13, 12, 10, 8</strong></p>

            <h3>Option 3: Point Buy</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg statroll pointbuy</div>
            <p>Build your stats with 27 points. All stats start at 8.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- AI DM -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="aidm">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-dragon" style="color: var(--color-danger-400);"></i> AI Dungeon Master</h2>
            <p>How the AI DM creates your adventure!</p>

            <h3>Starting a Session</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg session start</div>
            <p>The AI generates a unique scenario based on your character's class, race, level, and backstory.</p>

            <h3>Taking Actions</h3>
            <p>Just type normally after starting:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Actions:</strong> "I kick down the door"</li>
                <li><strong>Dialogue:</strong> "I ask the merchant about the missing shipment"</li>
                <li><strong>Combat:</strong> "I cast fireball at the enemies"</li>
                <li><strong>Exploration:</strong> "I examine the strange runes"</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How the DM Responds</h3>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Reads your action</strong> and determines response</li>
                <li><strong>Calls for rolls</strong> when needed (dice buttons appear)</li>
                <li><strong>Applies consequences</strong> - damage, healing, status effects</li>
                <li><strong>Tracks the story</strong> - NPCs remember you, locations persist</li>
                <li><strong>Uses D&D 5e rules</strong> - proper DCs, saves, combat rules</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>Difficulty Classes (DC)</h3>
            <table class="dc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>DC</th><th>Difficulty</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>5</td><td>Very Easy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>10</td><td>Easy</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>15</td><td>Medium</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>20</td><td>Hard</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>25</td><td>Very Hard</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>30</td><td>Nearly Impossible</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <!-- D&D 5e Mechanics -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="mechanics">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-cogs" style="color: var(--color-info-400);"></i> D&D 5e Mechanics</h2>
            <p>Death saves, exhaustion, inspiration, and more!</p>

            <h3>Death Saving Throws</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg condition deathsave</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Roll 10+ = Success, under 10 = Failure</li>
                <li><span class="danger-text"><strong>Nat 1</strong></span> = 2 failures</li>
                <li><span class="success-text"><strong>Nat 20</strong></span> = Regain 1 HP instantly!</li>
                <li>3 successes = Stabilized</li>
                <li>3 failures = <span class="danger-text">Dead</span></li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Exhaustion Levels</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg condition exhaustion</div>
            <table class="dc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Level</th><th>Effect</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>1</td><td>Disadvantage on ability checks</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2</td><td>Speed halved</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>3</td><td>Disadvantage on attacks/saves</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>4</td><td class="warning-text">HP maximum halved</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>5</td><td class="warning-text">Speed reduced to 0</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>6</td><td class="danger-text"><strong>Death</strong></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <h3>Inspiration</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg condition inspiration</div>
            <p>Granted by the DM for great roleplay. Use it for advantage on any roll!</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Rest & Recovery -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="rest">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-bed" style="color: var(--color-purple-400);"></i> Rest & Recovery</h2>
            <p>Heal up and restore your resources!</p>

            <h3>Short Rest (1 hour)</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg rest short hit_dice:2</div>
            <p>Spend hit dice to heal. Each die = 1dX + CON modifier.</p>

            <h3>Long Rest (8 hours)</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg rest long</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Full HP restored</li>
                <li>All spell slots/mana restored</li>
                <li>Recover half your hit dice</li>
                <li>Reduce exhaustion by 1</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Inventory -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="inventory">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-backpack" style="color: var(--color-warning-400);"></i> Inventory System</h2>
            <p>Manage your items and equipment!</p>

            <h3>View Inventory</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg inventory view</div>

            <h3>Equip/Unequip Items</h3>
            <div class="code-block">/rpg inventory equip item_id:5
/rpg inventory unequip item_id:5</div>

            <h3>Item Sources</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Loot drops</strong> from defeated enemies</li>
                <li><strong>Shop purchases</strong> with gold</li>
                <li><strong>Quest rewards</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Found during exploration</strong></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Story Continuity -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="continuity">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-book-open" style="color: var(--color-success-400);"></i> Story Continuity & Progression</h2>
            <p>How your adventure persists across sessions!</p>

            <h3>How Continuity Works</h3>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Session History</strong> - Narrative saved to database</li>
                <li><strong>Context Window</strong> - AI receives recent history</li>
                <li><strong>Character Memory</strong> - NPCs, locations tracked</li>
                <li><strong>Quest Progress</strong> - Active quests persist</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>What Gets Saved</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Your last actions and DM responses</li>
                <li>Current location and scene description</li>
                <li>Active NPCs and their dispositions</li>
                <li>Quest states (active, completed, failed)</li>
                <li>World events that have occurred</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>XP & Leveling</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Earn XP from combat, quests, and roleplay</li>
                <li>Level up automatically when XP threshold is met</li>
                <li>Each level increases: HP, proficiency bonus, and unlocks features</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Command Reference -->
        <div class="docs-section" id="commands">
            <h2><i class="fas fa-terminal" style="color: var(--color-primary-400);"></i> Command Reference</h2>

            <h3>Character Commands</h3>
            <table class="dc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Command</th><th>Description</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>/rpg character create</code></td><td>Make a new character</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>/rpg character view</code></td><td>View character sheet</td></tr>
